  "answer": "### Short Answer\n\n### Interpretation\nThe provision specifies the deadline for individuals to file their income tax returns, which is set for April 15 of each year. This applies to income earned in the previous taxable year, ensuring that taxpayers have a clear timeline for compliance.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers must be aware of this deadline to avoid penalties for late filing. It is crucial for individuals to prepare their income tax returns in advance of this date to ensure timely submission and compliance with tax obligations.",
